## R2.1 (B1) union-let widening smoke.
##
## A union-typed `let` (`x: Int | String = 5`) must lower to a runtime tagged
## `{tag, payload}` cell (reusing the enum boxed shape) instead of erasing the
## RHS to a bare scalar. B1 scope = CONSTRUCT + STORE + PASS-THROUGH only; the
## read/narrow side is B2, so this deliberately does NOT read the arm value back.
##
## Acceptance is by IR inspection (an `alloc` + a tag `store` at the union let)
## plus compile+run without crashing — there is no read side yet to assert the
## recovered value against.
def main(): Int
  x: Int | String = 5
  return 0
end
